CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ reference NTTP defaults to S::blank: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [temp.param]/4, [temp.arg.nontype]/1-2: a non-type template parameter may
have reference type, its argument designating a static-storage object (an
address constant).  This is the shape of util/reference_counting.h's
`template <typename T, const T &empty = T::blank>`, the root of the
ref_expr_set.cpp / rename_symbol.cpp / replace_symbol.cpp goto-cc cascade
(std::unordered_set/map of CBMC types).  The reference parameter keeps its
reference type, the reference argument is kept as the address of the static
object (not valuified), and template_suffix builds the instance name from the
object's identity.  assertion.2 FAILURE proves assertion.1 is non-vacuous.
